---

<IndustryDetailPage
  title="Mixed-Use Developments"
  seoTitle="Mixed-Use Construction Phoenix, AZ | Trinity Build Co."
  seoDescription="Mixed-use construction in Phoenix and across Arizona, coordinating residential, retail, office, sitework, shared systems, and phased turnover."
  eyebrow="Mixed-Use Construction"
  lede="Coordinated construction planning for developments that bring residential, retail, office, parking, and shared public spaces together in one program."
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroAlt="Mixed-use development under construction"
  heroPosition="center 48%"
  introTitle="One coordinated plan for every use."
  introParagraphs={[
    "Mixed-use developments combine building programs with different occupants, systems, schedules, access needs, and inspection paths. Their shared structures, utilities, circulation, parking, and public spaces make the connections between scopes just as important as the individual spaces themselves.",
    "Trinity Build Co. approaches the work as one coordinated program. Early planning identifies the interfaces, decision owners, long-lead items, tenant requirements, and phased milestones that influence cost, schedule, constructability, and occupancy across the development.",
  ]}
  capabilities={capabilities}
  supportImage={supportImage}
  supportAlt="Construction site entrance with perimeter fencing"
  supportPosition="center 52%"
  supportEyebrow="Coordinate the Interfaces"
  supportTitle="The intersections deserve their own plan."
  supportCopy="Clear scope boundaries, shared milestones, current decision logs, and coordinated site logistics help the team manage the points where residential, commercial, public, and infrastructure work come together."
  deliveryTitle="Keep every part of the program connected."
  deliveryCopy="Mixed-use work becomes more predictable when the team can see how one decision, handoff, or delay affects the other buildings, tenants, systems, and occupancy goals."
  deliveryItems={deliveryItems}
  faqs={faqs}
/>
